# Where fetch_drivers.py looks for images. Copy this file to `.env` (it is not committed).
# You need at least one of the two options. More in scripts/README.md

# Option 1: URL templates (the simple one). Separated by spaces, tried in order for each driver:
# the first one that returns a transparent image wins. Placeholders:
#   {id} id in RaceDex   {tla} abbreviation (VER)   {ref} reference (MAXVER01)   {year} a season of the driver
DRIVERS_URL_TEMPLATES=https://example.com/drivers/{year}/{ref}.png https://example.org/headshots/{year}/{tla}.png

# Option 2: sitemap(s), separated by spaces. For sites whose image URLs don't follow a pattern.
# It goes first, and the templates are used for the drivers that it doesn't have.
# DRIVERS_SITEMAP_URL=https://example.net/drivers-sitemap.xml
# DRIVERS_PAGE_PATH=/drivers/        # part of the URL that the pages of the drivers have in common

# Where the drivers are read from: the address of a folder with the CSV files of the RaceDex API (optional)
# RACEDEX_DATA_URL=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/enrique-lozano/F1-World-API/main/data/csv
